            <div xml:id="d842-a3">

                <pb facs="0984" n="890" xml:id="pg890"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 1019.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Affidavit of Mrs. Mary E. Barnum.</hi></head>
                <p>On November 11 we watched the soldiers on the hill opposite, stationed there with
                    a cannon, apparently to guard the approach to the city. But when we saw that the
                    Kurds were allowed to pass by the soldiers with only a few minutes’ delay, we
                    felt that neither we nor the people were to be protected. After we fled to the
                    college building I saw a soldier with a load of plunder on his back near our
                    premises, and a rug looked like one of ours.</p>
                <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mary E. Barnum.</hi></p>
                <p>I hereby certify upon oath that the above statement made by me is true and
                    correct.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mary E. Barnum.</hi></signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harpoot</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-09-17"><hi rendition="#italic">September 17,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Sworn by Mrs. Barnum, at Harpoot, on this 17th day of September, before
                        me.</p>
                    <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Raphael A.
                        Fontana.</hi></signed></closer>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
